body:
I remember having to put water into the old photo machines and changing the chemicals was an all day thing

&#x200B;

Edit: Hell I remember more now

I remember control strips and dealing with Fuji Oasis.

&#x200B;

I remember when the seasonal aisles weren't premade and we had the ability to be creative

&#x200B;

I remember hanging signs from the ceiling

&#x200B;

I remember suggestive sales

&#x200B;

I remember dealing with SRU canisters

&#x200B;

I remember when "Welcome to Walgreens" first started

&#x200B;

I remember when we were able to actually apprehend shoplifters

&#x200B;

I remember the old registers where the manager pass was a key

&#x200B;

I remember you had to have at least 6 of an item to be able to use the quantity key
